<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21556" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illōtus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inl-</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illautus</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illūtus</span></b> ), a, um, adj.
		in-lotus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>unwashed</i>, <i>uncleaned</i>, <i>unclean</i>, <i>dirty.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b> </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> Form illotus: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illotis manibus aliquid tractare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 1, 2, 103</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">toralia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 4, 84</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">echini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 8, 52</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cochleae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					30, 6, 16, § 49</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">faex vini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					23, 2, 31, § 63</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inlotus sudor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 443</span></i>
			 (Rib.).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b> Form illautus, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 1, 2,
			23</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(g).</b>
			Form illutus: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinacei,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 147</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			Prov.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illotis manibus or pedibus facere aliquid,</span>”
				<i>to underlake a thing without due preparation</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					1, 2, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Gell. 1, 9, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">17, 5</span></i>
			<i>fin.</i>, <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 24,
				§ 12</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: illotus sermo, Auct. Decl. in <i><span class="en">Sall.
				1, § 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
